Xray-core Corresponding Source Notice
=====================================

The unmodified Xray-core executable in the proxyscene offline bundles is from:

- Release: v26.9.9 (upstream prerelease, selected after four-architecture verification)
- Source commit: 52a412d9e2f5c2a5142b1b4e2ab3771dacb8b120
- Upstream source: https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core/tree/v26.9.9
- Upstream build Go version recorded in the ELF: go1.27.1

The same immutable proxyscene GitHub Release carries
`xray_source_v26.9.9.tar.gz`. Its SHA256 is listed in that Release's
`checksums.txt`. The source archive contains the exact Xray-core source module
and the source module zip, go.mod, and module metadata for every Go module
recorded in the redistributed ELF by `go version -m`. It also contains the
license and notice collection used by the binary bundle.

The upstream Linux build command is recorded in Xray-core's release workflow.
For ordinary Linux targets it builds `./main` with CGO disabled, trim paths,
disabled VCS stamping, `-gcflags=all=-l=4`, and linker flags that set the Xray
build identifier and remove the Go build ID. See the exact source and workflow
at the commit above for the authoritative build instructions.

proxyscene does not modify the Xray-core executable. The Xray-core project is
licensed under MPL-2.0. The linked dependency set includes GPL-3.0-or-later,
LGPL-3.0-with-linking-exception, MPL-2.0, and permissively licensed modules;
their exact versions, Go module sums, licenses, and notices are recorded in
`THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES-Xray`.

The generated proxyscene routing configuration does not use `geoip.dat` or
`geosite.dat`. Those data files are not extracted, installed, or redistributed
by current proxyscene releases.
